(7) To manage the department payroll within the compensation appropriation levels;
(8) To serve as secretary to the planning commission, as now existing or hereinafter amended;
(9) To sign all decisions, resolutions, reports, and recommendations of the planning commission, pursuant to the by-laws of the planning commission, as now existing or hereinafter amended;
(10) To act as technical consultant to the planning commission on planning issues; To represent the planning commission through communications with county departments, elected and appointed officials, and other public, quasi governmental agencies, cities, and the private sector;
(11) To recommend to the planning commission, at least on an annual basis, any revision to the planning commission's by-laws; and, to perform other duties as directed by the board of commissioners within the expertise of the director.
(12) To present a proposed amendment at regular meetings of the board of commissioners, at which meetings such proposed amendment shall be considered for adoption by the board of commissioners.
(13) Advertise and or post notices of meetings and proceedings as required by law.
